WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.164 --> 00:00:01.012
- So, John.

00:00:01.012 --> 00:00:03.606
People are always talking
about the Constitution.

00:00:03.606 --> 00:00:04.770
But, the Constitution

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:08.690
was not the first founding
document of the United States.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:10.600
What were the Articles of Confederation,

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:11.909
and why did they need to get replaced?

00:00:11.909 --> 00:00:13.580
- Well, the Articles of Confederation

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.320
were the first loose set of rules

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.430
to govern these 13 states,

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:18.470
but they were a mess.

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:20.300
Essentially, they allowed the states

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.773
to be kind of their own
little sovereign islands.

00:00:22.773 --> 00:00:25.740
So, it was not a united nation.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:29.150
It was like an Archipelago of islands.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:30.470
And, the reason they were a mess.

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:31.303
There's a couple of things.

00:00:31.303 --> 00:00:32.383
One,

00:00:32.383 --> 00:00:36.410
when they tried to repay the
Revolutionary War soldiers,

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:38.190
Congress and Washington
with very little power,

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:39.700
had to go to the states and say,

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:41.970
please give us some money so
we can repay the soldiers.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:43.450
A lot of the states said, no thank you.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:44.790
We're not going to do that.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:45.770
Then if you had a river

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:48.000
that rolled through
several different states,

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.360
and you wanted to have a trade agreement

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:50.670
with the Spanish, for example,

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.199
to use that river and trade along it,

00:00:52.199 --> 00:00:54.280
then the government didn't have one way

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:55.520
to negotiate with the Spanish.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.080
Individual states had to do it,

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:59.700
and individual states
had different interests.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.760
Some wanted to trade with the Spanish.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.190
Some didn't want to trade at all.

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:06.300
And so, how do you get those
states to agree on something?

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.330
There was also not universal coinage.

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:10.242
The states all made their
own money and differently.

00:01:10.242 --> 00:01:12.750
Well, states might print a bunch of money

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:14.200
in order to payoff some debts,

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.338
and then the money in one state

00:01:15.338 --> 00:01:17.390
is worth less than the money in another,

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:18.940
who regulates all of that?

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:21.800
So, commerce, and
industry, and self-defense.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:23.811
There was no way to raise
an army an pay for it.

00:01:23.811 --> 00:01:27.351
So, the nation was
crumbling before they got to

00:01:27.351 --> 00:01:29.930
Philadelphia in 1787.

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:30.763
- And to your point,

00:01:30.763 --> 00:01:33.300
in most countries the parts of the country

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.560
are called things like provinces,

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:36.450
but ours are states,

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:40.940
because they view themselves
as individual countries.

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:41.773
- Absolutely,

00:01:41.773 --> 00:01:44.523
and because of course, the
Articles of Confederation

00:01:44.523 --> 00:01:47.070
had been formed in the wake of this fear,

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:49.270
and the experience of
the fear of a monarchy.

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:51.720
So, they wanted personal liberty,

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:54.863
and get the monarchy and national control,

00:01:54.863 --> 00:01:56.110
throw it all away,

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:59.300
because they believe that
once you consolidate control,

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:02.300
in a national government of any kind,

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.610
that it would trample liberty.

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:05.680
And so, after having fought a revolution

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:07.280
for the purposes of liberating the people,

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:08.690
you're not gonna design a government

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:11.060
that then stomps down on that liberty.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:12.868
So, they created something
that gave the states

00:02:12.868 --> 00:02:14.560
lots of flexibility,

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.390
and then that flexibility
allowed everybody

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:17.930
to go off in their different directions.

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:19.520
- So, Articles of Confederation,

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:20.920
maybe too much independence

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.600
for the individual states.

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:25.380
So, it seems like there
was a consensus to fix it.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.472
What was the central debate

00:02:26.472 --> 00:02:28.670
when they decided to fix it?

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:31.820
- Well, there was a
consensus it had to be fixed,

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:34.310
but when they got to Philadelphia.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.010
First of all, Rhode Island was invited

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:36.990
and said no thank you,

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.140
so 12 of the 13 states showed up.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:41.520
And, they knew they wanted
to centralize things.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.200
But, what did that mean?

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.960
And, did it mean one president,
or a council of presidents?

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:47.560
Did it mean a strong Congress?

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:48.393
How strong?

00:02:48.393 --> 00:02:49.890
Could they tell states what to do?

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:50.723
Well, if they did that

00:02:50.723 --> 00:02:52.938
then they were acting just
like George III had acted.

00:02:52.938 --> 00:02:56.000
So, they had to iron
out all of these issues

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.449
to bring enough central control,

00:02:57.449 --> 00:02:59.510
and enough quick movement of government,

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:01.326
that it could address national problems,

00:03:01.326 --> 00:03:02.680
but not so much that it

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:04.800
trampled and stomped on that liberty.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.840
And, that was the constant debate.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.420
Constantly trying to figure out

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:09.690
how to keep the balance between

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:11.540
giving enough national power,

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:12.690
but enough liberty.

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:14.690
And that, some of the
biggest fights included

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:16.880
fights over slavery, North versus South,

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:18.970
fights over big states
versus small states.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:21.200
Who has representation in
this national government,

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.430
and how do you figure that out?

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:23.812
And then of course, the question of

00:03:23.812 --> 00:03:25.910
do we want a president?

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:27.160
Will it be a single person,

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.300
and how the dickens do
we elect that person?

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:30.900
Which led us to the Electoral College,

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.810
which has had some bumpy history.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:34.940
- And, where do you think we ended up?

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.473
If on a scale of zero to 10.

00:03:36.473 --> 00:03:40.440
If was zero was a complete,
you know, independent states,

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:42.340
and 10 is a federal government

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:43.450
that just controls everything.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:44.780
Where do you think the US Constitution

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:46.780
ended up relative to the
Articles of Confederation?

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:49.770
- Well, in September of 1787,

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:52.698
when it gets September 17th, 1787.

00:03:52.698 --> 00:03:55.670
When the new Constitution gets voted on,

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:57.810
it is a stronger national document

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:00.140
that has basically three main parts.

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:02.418
One, the people are at the
heart and center of it.

00:04:02.418 --> 00:04:04.812
It is the people who
are the representatives,

00:04:04.812 --> 00:04:07.041
or at the center of the
republican government.

00:04:07.041 --> 00:04:09.410
The second thing is that
the national government

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:11.630
can tell states what to
do in some instances.

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:14.488
Those instances are
circumscribed, but it can happen.

00:04:14.488 --> 00:04:16.390
The states have to fall in line.

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:17.280
That was very new,

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:18.510
and there is this thing called

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:20.040
a presidency which is created.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:21.130
Single person,

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:23.810
created really in the
mold of George Washington.

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:25.321
So, it is a nationalized government,

00:04:25.321 --> 00:04:29.369
but with a strong
attention to this question

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:32.800
of protecting liberty through
a balance of power system,

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:36.007
so that both the national government has

00:04:36.007 --> 00:04:37.383
checks and balances,

00:04:37.383 --> 00:04:38.950
and also the relationship

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:40.490
between the federal government
and the state government

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:42.760
has a number of checks and balances.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.330
So, even though they went in
a more centralized direction,

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:48.780
they were constantly attentive
to this idea of liberty,

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:50.048
keeping it free in the states,

00:04:50.048 --> 00:04:51.964
and not messing with them too much

00:04:51.964 --> 00:04:54.900
in their effort to get some
kind of centralized control.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:56.010
- So, it sounds like they might have gone

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:57.858
from a one or a two with the
Articles of Confederation,

00:04:57.858 --> 00:05:00.300
to maybe a seven?

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.133
Six?

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:01.966
- Well, they went,

00:05:01.966 --> 00:05:04.160
I think they went from a one or two

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:07.220
to maybe a five or a six,

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:08.759
which has now moved.

00:05:08.759 --> 00:05:09.820
- Over time.

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:11.200
- Over time,

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.389
closer to maybe an eight or nine.

00:05:13.389 --> 00:05:14.423
- Fascinating.

